\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Timely Happy, Timely Wise,
\par Hearts that with rising morn arise,
\par Eyes that the beam celestial view
\par Which evermore makes all things new.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. New every morning is the love
\par Our wakening and uprising prove,
\par Through sleep and darkness safely brought,
\par Restored to life, and power, and thought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. New mercies each returning day
\par Hover around us while we pray;
\par New perils  past, new sins forgiven,
\par New thoughts of God, new hopes of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If on our daily course our mind
\par Be set to hallow all we find,
\par New treasures still of countless price
\par God will provide for sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Old friends, old scenes, will lovelier be,
\par As more of heaven in each we see;
\par Some softening gleam of love and prayer
\par Shall dawn on every cross and care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The trivial round, the common task,
\par Will furnish all we ought to ask;
\par Room to deny ourselves, a road
\par To bring us daily nearer God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Only, O Lord, in Thy great love,
\par Fit us for perfect rest above;
\par And help us, this and every day,
\par To live more nearly as we pray.
\par                         Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
